## Ruida

# Dealing with driver feature gaps

## Problem description

Ruida does not support raster lines in arbitrary directions. We should add a driver flag that indicates support for non-horizontal Raster lines, and if false then our raster producer should disable the angle and cross hatch options.
This needs to be done carefully: A user with multiple machines may switch between machines with a project already having these options active, so the rejection must happen on two levels: UI, and production.
And we need a way for production side to indicate to the UI that an enabled feature is not supported by the current machine.

Also, unlike Grbl, Ruida automatically adds overscan. This requires a similar flag to resolve, which should then disable the Overscan transformer in Rayforge. This needs to be handled similar to the above.

